{"id":"study-timetable","title":"A study timetable you'll actually follow","subject":"Study skills","label":"Study skills","exams":[],"language":"en","seconds":166,"duration":166.29,"audio":"voice.mp3","words":451,"sections":[{"id":"hook","title":"The puzzle","start":0,"end":14.245},{"id":"explain","title":"Core steps","start":14.245,"end":53.515},{"id":"explain2","title":"More steps","start":53.515,"end":83.645},{"id":"example","title":"Worked example","start":83.645,"end":107.565},{"id":"check","title":"Quick check","start":107.565,"end":119.905},{"id":"answer","title":"Answer","start":119.905,"end":126.915},{"id":"mistakes","title":"Common mistakes","start":126.915,"end":140.585},{"id":"recap","title":"Recap","start":140.585,"end":166.29}],"lines":[{"s":0,"a":0.5,"b":7.74,"text":"Why do most study timetables collapse by Wednesday? You made a plan, felt hopeful, then one busy evening broke it.","w":[0.54,0.8,0.94,1.22,1.52,2.12,2.58,2.76,3.78,3.92,4.08,4.14,4.84,5.1,5.98,6.3,6.5,6.9,7.22,7.54]},{"s":0,"a":8.04,"b":13.82,"text":"I'm Kora. In the next three minutes, you'll build a timetable you can actually follow, even on a bad day.","w":[8.12,8.3,8.94,9.04,9.14,9.38,9.64,10.3,10.54,10.8,10.86,11.42,11.54,11.72,12.08,12.84,13.1,13.22,13.28,13.54]},{"s":1,"a":14.67,"b":21.57,"text":"Most timetables fail because they are wishes. Every hour is filled, there is no rest, and no room for a bad day.","w":[14.76,15.06,15.74,16.12,16.4,16.56,16.7,17.84,18.1,18.48,18.62,19.2,19.4,19.56,19.78,20.22,20.34,20.56,20.84,20.98,21.06,21.3]},{"s":1,"a":21.87,"b":28.51,"text":"First, list your fixed things: school, chores, travel, sleep, worship, sport. Find your real free slots.","w":[21.9,22.22,22.42,22.6,22.86,23.58,24.28,24.74,25.26,25.66,26.16,26.94,27.16,27.36,27.7,27.96]},{"s":1,"a":28.81,"b":36.99,"text":"Second, list your subjects and rate each one weak, okay or strong. Give weak subjects more slots, not all of them.","w":[28.94,30,30.26,30.48,31.04,31.18,31.56,31.86,32.06,32.8,33.24,33.4,34.26,34.52,34.8,35.3,35.52,36.26,36.56,36.74,36.82]},{"s":1,"a":37.29,"b":42.82,"text":"Third, use short focused blocks of twenty-five to forty-five minutes, with a five to ten minute break.","w":[37.29,37.67,37.88,38.2,38.63,39.01,39.17,39.81,39.97,40.57,41.05,41.32,41.42,41.69,41.85,42.07,42.44]},{"s":1,"a":43.12,"b":48.54,"text":"Name the task, not just the subject. Say ten questions on quadratic equations, not Maths.","w":[43.2,43.44,43.54,44.12,44.32,44.5,44.62,45.48,45.68,45.94,46.42,46.54,47.02,47.82,48.06]},{"s":1,"a":48.84,"b":53.09,"text":"A good timetable has breathing room, so one missed block does not ruin the week.","w":[48.88,48.98,49.22,49.8,50.04,50.42,50.84,51.1,51.3,51.58,51.9,52.14,52.4,52.66,52.76]},{"s":2,"a":53.94,"b":57.39,"text":"Fourth, put the hardest subject where your energy is highest.","w":[53.94,54.7,54.9,55.06,55.42,55.92,56.1,56.32,56.72,56.86]},{"s":2,"a":57.69,"b":62.95,"text":"Fifth, schedule reviews: revisit a topic the next day, and again within a week.","w":[57.74,58.6,59.04,59.92,60.46,60.52,60.92,61.04,61.28,61.84,61.96,62.28,62.56,62.64]},{"s":2,"a":63.25,"b":67.7,"text":"Sixth, leave one or two empty catch-up slots and one free evening each week.","w":[63.25,63.65,64,64.23,64.41,64.64,64.98,65.5,65.85,66.08,66.31,66.6,67.06,67.35]},{"s":2,"a":68,"b":75.27,"text":"Seventh, start small, even two blocks a day. Tie study to something you already do, like right after dinner.","w":[68.1,68.9,69.22,70.04,70.3,70.5,70.86,70.94,71.72,72.04,72.38,72.5,72.82,73.04,73.42,74.18,74.46,74.72,74.98]},{"s":2,"a":75.57,"b":78.57,"text":"Tick off each block, and review the plan every Sunday.","w":[75.58,75.84,76.08,76.3,76.96,77.1,77.4,77.5,77.9,78.16]},{"s":2,"a":78.87,"b":83.22,"text":"The catch-up slot stays empty on purpose, so you can use it when life happens.","w":[78.87,79.09,79.59,79.86,80.19,80.52,80.69,81.18,81.35,81.57,81.79,82.01,82.17,82.45,82.72]},{"s":3,"a":84.07,"b":87.52,"text":"Take a student free from six to nine in the evening on weekdays.","w":[84.08,84.32,84.4,84.78,85.04,85.3,85.56,85.7,86.06,86.16,86.34,86.74,86.86]},{"s":3,"a":87.82,"b":91.56,"text":"Plan two forty-minute blocks, with a break and dinner between them.","w":[87.82,88.09,88.31,89.03,89.47,89.75,89.86,90.19,90.41,90.79,91.23]},{"s":3,"a":91.86,"b":97.36,"text":"So: six to six forty, weak subject first. Then a break and dinner. Then the second block.","w":[91.98,92.74,92.98,93.12,93.36,94,94.24,94.62,95.28,95.48,95.54,95.82,95.94,96.52,96.7,96.82,97.1]},{"s":3,"a":97.66,"b":101.15,"text":"After that, add a ten-minute review of yesterday's topic.","w":[97.66,98.02,98.38,98.62,98.74,99.41,99.83,100.01,100.73]},{"s":3,"a":101.45,"b":102.69,"text":"Keep Friday evening off.","w":[101.48,101.78,102.22,102.56]},{"s":3,"a":102.99,"b":107.14,"text":"That gives two solid blocks, a short review, and a calm finish.","w":[103.02,103.24,103.52,103.78,104.16,104.92,105.04,105.3,106.1,106.24,106.32,106.68]},{"s":4,"a":107.99,"b":116.53,"text":"Which is the better timetable entry: Chemistry, seven to nine, or seven to seven forty, ten mole calculations, then check answers, and why?","w":[108,108.2,108.32,108.46,108.8,109.44,109.98,110.68,110.94,111.08,111.64,111.82,112.12,112.24,112.54,113.22,113.5,113.76,114.86,115.1,115.42,115.94,116.14]},{"s":4,"a":116.98,"b":119.48,"text":"Pause here and try it. I'll wait.","w":[117,117.34,117.88,118.02,118.28,118.94,119.12]},{"s":5,"a":120.33,"b":126.49,"text":"The second entry is better because it names a clear task and a short block, so you know exactly when to start and stop.","w":[120.36,120.52,120.86,121.22,121.34,121.68,121.96,122.06,122.36,122.48,122.82,123.28,123.4,123.5,123.78,124.4,124.56,124.68,124.86,125.4,125.6,125.72,126.06,126.2]},{"s":6,"a":127.34,"b":131.79,"text":"Don't copy a friend's timetable; your free slots and weak subjects are different.","w":[127.34,127.58,127.92,128.04,128.36,129.32,129.54,129.82,130.32,130.5,130.76,131.34,131.46]},{"s":6,"a":132.09,"b":135.99,"text":"Don't plan six hours with no breaks; use short blocks and rest.","w":[132.12,132.4,132.72,132.94,133.28,133.44,133.6,134.46,134.64,134.9,135.42,135.58]},{"s":6,"a":136.29,"b":140.16,"text":"Don't give up after one missed day; use your catch-up slot and continue.","w":[136.29,136.61,136.87,137.03,137.35,137.56,137.93,138.2,138.41,138.68,139.15,139.42,139.63]},{"s":7,"a":141.01,"b":146.33,"text":"Recap: list fixed things first, then rate subjects and give weak ones more slots.","w":[141.08,141.9,142.24,142.58,142.9,143.62,143.86,144.12,144.76,144.9,145.16,145.44,145.66,145.86]},{"s":7,"a":146.63,"b":151.34,"text":"Use short named blocks, hardest subject at high energy, and schedule reviews.","w":[146.74,147.02,147.28,147.52,148.34,148.68,149.1,149.22,149.46,150.22,150.4,150.8]},{"s":7,"a":151.64,"b":156.51,"text":"Leave catch-up slots, start small, tick off blocks, and review every Sunday.","w":[151.64,152.02,152.59,153.03,153.41,153.85,154.17,154.42,154.93,155.18,155.62,156]},{"s":7,"a":156.81,"b":161,"text":"Top tip: tie study to a daily habit, like right after dinner.","w":[156.86,157.18,158.02,158.3,158.66,158.8,158.88,159.2,159.96,160.22,160.48,160.72]},{"s":7,"a":161.3,"b":165.69,"text":"Build one small timetable this week with Knowzone, and keep it kind to real life.","w":[161.32,161.72,161.92,162.24,162.74,162.96,163.16,163.36,164.14,164.3,164.54,164.68,165,165.18,165.46]}],"scenes":[{"at":0.25,"heading":"The problem","items":[{"at":0.4,"kind":"text","text":"Most timetables collapse by Wednesday"},{"at":7.94,"kind":"text","text":"Build one you can follow, even on a bad day"}]},{"at":14.42,"heading":"Core steps 1-3","items":[{"at":14.57,"kind":"text","text":"Most timetables are wishes: full, no rest, no bad-day room"},{"at":21.77,"kind":"term","text":"Fixed things","detail":"school, chores, travel, sleep, worship, sport"},{"at":28.71,"kind":"term","text":"Rate subjects","detail":"weak, okay or strong; give weak subjects more slots"}]},{"at":37.04,"heading":"Blocks and breathing room","items":[{"at":37.19,"kind":"text","text":"Short blocks: 25-45 min + 5-10 min break"},{"at":43.02,"kind":"text","text":"Name the task, not just the subject"},{"at":48.74,"kind":"text","text":"Leave breathing room for missed blocks"}]},{"at":53.69,"heading":"More steps 4-6","items":[{"at":53.84,"kind":"text","text":"Hardest subject at highest energy"},{"at":57.59,"kind":"text","text":"Review next day, then within a week"},{"at":63.15,"kind":"text","text":"1-2 catch-up slots + 1 free evening"}]},{"at":67.75,"heading":"Start small and review","items":[{"at":67.9,"kind":"text","text":"Start with 2 blocks/day; tie to a habit"},{"at":75.47,"kind":"text","text":"Tick off blocks; review plan every Sunday"},{"at":78.77,"kind":"text","text":"Catch-up stays empty on purpose"}]},{"at":83.82,"heading":"Worked example: 6-9 pm","items":[{"at":83.97,"kind":"text","text":"Free: 6-9 pm on weekdays"},{"at":87.72,"kind":"text","text":"2 × 40-min blocks + break + dinner"},{"at":91.76,"kind":"text","text":"6:00-6:40 weak subject; break + dinner; block 2"}]},{"at":97.41,"heading":"Worked example: finish","items":[{"at":97.56,"kind":"text","text":"Add 10-min review of yesterday"},{"at":101.35,"kind":"text","text":"Friday evening off"},{"at":102.89,"kind":"text","text":"2 blocks + short review + calm finish"}]},{"at":107.56,"heading":"Quick check","items":[{"at":107.56,"kind":"question","text":"Which is the better timetable entry: \"Chemistry, 7 to 9\" or \"7:00 to 7:40, ten mole calculations, then check answers\"? Why?"}]},{"at":120.08,"heading":"Answer","items":[{"at":120.23,"kind":"text","text":"Second entry is better"},{"at":120.23,"kind":"text","text":"Clear task + short block: know start and stop"}]},{"at":127.09,"heading":"Common mistakes","items":[{"at":127.24,"kind":"wrong","text":"Copy a friend's timetable"},{"at":131.99,"kind":"wrong","text":"Plan 6 hours with no breaks"},{"at":136.19,"kind":"wrong","text":"Give up after one missed day"}]},{"at":140.76,"heading":"Recap","items":[{"at":140.91,"kind":"text","text":"Fixed things first; rate subjects; weak get more slots"},{"at":146.53,"kind":"text","text":"Short named blocks; hardest at high energy; reviews"},{"at":151.54,"kind":"text","text":"Catch-up slots; start small; tick off; Sunday review"},{"at":156.71,"kind":"tip","text":"Tie study to a daily habit, like right after dinner"},{"at":161.2,"kind":"text","text":"Knowzone: build one small timetable this week"}]}],"check":{"at":119.73,"seconds":10,"question":"Which is the better timetable entry: \"Chemistry, 7 to 9\" or \"7:00 to 7:40, ten mole calculations, then check answers\"? Why?","answer":"The second entry: it names a clear task and a short block, so you know exactly when to start and stop."},"fps":30,"mouth":"","level":"","credits":[],"voice":"qwen3-tts-12hz-1.7b (cloned voice)"}